# shortener: link shortener in Python (stdlib + SQLite) with a static page.
# Components, globs, exclusions, relations and anchored rules. Anchors come after the period: ^file#symbol.

# --- components and the files that implement them
The program "server" is implemented in "shortener/**".
The program "server" contains the module "server.routes", the module "server.entry", the module "server.static", the module "server.stats", the module "server.rules", the module "server.store" and the module "server.code".
The module "server.routes" is implemented in "shortener/server.py".
The module "server.entry" is implemented in "shortener/__main__.py".
The module "server.static" is implemented in "shortener/static.py".
The module "server.stats" is implemented in "shortener/stats.py".
The module "server.rules" is implemented in "shortener/{validate,rate_limit}.py".
The module "server.store" is implemented in "shortener/store.py".
The module "server.code" is implemented in "shortener/code.py".
The page "page" is implemented in "static/**".
The file "gitignore" is implemented in ".gitignore".
The test suite "tests" is implemented in "tests/**".

# --- relations
The page "page" uses the module "server.routes".
The module "server.entry" uses the module "server.routes" and the module "server.store".
The module "server.routes" uses the module "server.rules", the module "server.store", the module "server.static" and the module "server.stats".
The module "server.static" reads the page "page".
The module "server.stats" uses the module "server.store".
The module "server.store" uses the module "server.code".
The module "server.store" writes the file "shortener.db".
The file "gitignore" skips the file "shortener.db".
The test suite "tests" uses the module "server.routes", the module "server.rules", the module "server.store" and the module "server.code".

# --- environment and headers
The module "server.routes" reads the environment variable "SHORTENER_ADMIN".
Note: with SHORTENER_ADMIN unset, deletion always refuses; the value is compared in constant time (hmac.compare_digest).
The module "server.routes" reads the header "X-Admin-Token", the header "Content-Length" and the header "Referer".
The module "server.routes" writes the header "Location" and the header "Content-Type".

# --- routes and responses
The module "server.routes" serves the route "POST /api/links", the route "GET /{code}", the route "GET /api/links/{code}/stats", the route "DELETE /api/links/{code}" and the route "GET /".
Note: "/" and "/static/app.js" come from the allow list in static.py; the code has 6 base62 characters.
The route "POST /api/links" responds with the status code "201".
The route "POST /api/links" responds with the status code "400".
Note: 400 for a body that is not a JSON object, an invalid URL or an invalid ttl.
The route "POST /api/links" responds with the status code "429".
Note: token bucket per IP: 10 creations per 60 s window.
The route "GET /{code}" redirects to the value "link url".
Note: responds 302 with the Location header and records the click.
The route "GET /{code}" responds with the status code "404".
The route "GET /{code}" responds with the status code "410".
The route "GET /api/links/{code}/stats" responds with the status code "200".
The route "GET /api/links/{code}/stats" responds with the status code "404".
The route "DELETE /api/links/{code}" responds with the status code "204".
The route "DELETE /api/links/{code}" responds with the status code "403".
The route "DELETE /api/links/{code}" responds with the status code "404".

# --- numbers and times
The value "body" is at most 4096.
Note: BODY_LIMIT, in bytes; a larger or negative Content-Length is refused with 400.
The value "ttl" is greater than 0.
Note: in seconds; without a ttl the link never expires.
The value "tokens" is at most the value "capacity".
Note: the bucket refills at capacity/window tokens per second and never exceeds the capacity.

# --- rules (anchored)
# DELETE without a valid token responds 403 before looking up the link; with SHORTENER_ADMIN unset it always refuses
If the value "admin token" is empty, the route "DELETE /api/links/{code}" responds with the status code "403". ^shortener/server.py#do_DELETE
# an expired link responds 410 and records no click
If the record "link" times out, the route "GET /{code}" responds with the status code "410". ^shortener/server.py#do_GET
If the record "link" times out, the module "server.routes" never writes the record "click".
# only allow-listed paths are read; any other gives 404
The module "server.static" never serves the file "shortener.db". ^shortener/static.py#read_page
# every store write takes the lock and commits before returning
The module "server.store" is protected by the lock "write lock". ^shortener/store.py#Store
